node_modules
# Build output: the production build and every look-page / lab build.
#
# ONE PATTERN, not a hand-kept list. This was ~60 lines spread over four blocks
# and it drifted badly: 8,164 files across 21 of these directories were tracked
# anyway — mostly copies of public/ (4,437 mp3, 2,063 glb) duplicated into each
# build. A name added to the list after its directory was first committed does
# nothing, because .gitignore cannot untrack; that is how the drift hid.
#
# The rule for all of them: the PAGE and its runner are tracked, what they
# generate is not. Same for the layout audit (npm run layout), the shader lab
# (its page, apply tool and tools/looks/shader-lab.json are tracked) and the
# pose lab, whose build alone is 134MB.
#
# dist-clap-lab used to be deliberately checked in, to avoid a tracked
# directory sitting quietly ignored. It is untracked now, so the exception is
# gone and the pattern covers it like the rest.
dist
dist-*
seal-survivor-itch.zip
.DS_Store
.env
# Wrangler's local state, one directory per worker — `wrangler dev --local`
# keeps a whole simulated KV in here. A pattern per worker rather than a bare
# `.wrangler`, which would also swallow one at the repo root if it ever mattered.
server/.wrangler
server/playtest/.wrangler

# Recorded playtest runs — session data, not source. `npm run playtest`
# reads this; delete it any time to start a fresh body of evidence. Runs pulled
# from the live site land here too, as remote.jsonl.
#
# LEADING SLASH REQUIRED. Unanchored, this matches a directory called
# `playtest` at ANY depth — which silently swallowed the whole of
# `server/playtest/` (the collection worker) the moment it was written. Nothing
# reports that: the files exist, the tests pass, and they are simply absent
# from every clone.
/playtest/

# The rendered sound atlas — a megabyte of it is base64'd audio, regenerated
# by `npm run sfx:atlas`. The data file it is built from (tools/sfx-atlas.json)
# IS tracked, because a diff of that is how you see what a change did to the
# sound bank.
tools/sfx-atlas.html

# The grid shader compile check, written by tools/grid-shader-check.mjs and
# opened in a browser. Generated, and only useful for the minute you look at it.
.grid-shader-check.html
.water-shader-check.html
.impact-shader-check.html
.biolum-shader-check.html
.goo-shader-check.html
.net-shader-check.html
.outline-shader-check.html
.goal-shader-check.html

# WebGL renders for the Model Atlas — regenerated by tools/atlas-render, never committed
tools/atlas-render/shots/

# Pre-WebP copies of the models, written by `npm run webp --write`. Outside
# public/ on purpose: vite copies that directory into the build wholesale, so a
# backup left beside the models ships to every player. Delete once a converted
# model has been seen in game — nothing can regenerate a source texture.
.model-orig/

# the hive look sheets are generated (npm run look:hive / look:stacks)
hive-look.html
hive-stacks.html

# The seeded design canvas (npm-less: tools from the /design skill). The
# .dc.html artboards and canvas.json ARE the source and are tracked; this is
# the 2.2MB published page they get seeded into, which is regenerated on every
# publish — same rule as the look-page builds above.
design/gameover-canvas/seal-survivor-game-over.html
release

# Sealitaire (rive/sealitaire): the CLI writes its .riv, .rev, logs and every
# screenshot here. Regenerated by `npm run sealitaire:build`.
rive/sealitaire/build/
